{
  "comment": "Where the schemas that kubeconform reads come from (09/T3; S19). Every source is a file at a commit of a public repository, fetched from raw.githubusercontent.com; the lock (schemas.lock.json) holds the sha256 of every source and of every file made from it. A commit is chosen at least 14 days after it was made (dependency rule 15, applied to data too). To move one: change the commit (and the tag, which is only for the reader), run `python3 -B -I deploy/schemas/fetch.py` on a developer machine, read the diff of the lock and of the schemas, and commit them together.",
